ernary\", \"concept\": \"Kenny code / ternary 3-groups (m p f) and other fixed-width ternary carriers\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Bacon-like group code: 3 symbols x width 3 = 27 values -> a-z; ternary digits 0/1/2 groups -> letters or nibbles. Table decode + fixtures; CyberChef has no Kenny op.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"chuck-norris-unary\", \"concept\": \"Chuck Norris unary (blocks of 0: `0`=1-run, `00`=0-run, then the run length)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Binary carrier with only `0` and spaces; 7-bit ASCII classic, maybe 4-bit nibbles over hex in this lane. Strict branch: only `0` and single spaces, even token count, first token of each pair `0` or `00`.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"charcode-radix\", \"concept\": \"char codes / nibbles in base 3, 4, 5, 7 (fixed-width digit groups)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Numeric carriers between binary and octal: quaternary 4-digit groups (0-3), ternary 5-digit (0-2), base-5/7. Detect radix = max digit + 1, width = constant token length; value 32-126 -> chr, <16 -> hex nibble.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"base92\", \"concept\": \"base92\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"chepy from_base92 / CyberChef From Base92 decode it; cue = printable minus double-quote and backtick.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"base65536\", \"concept\": \"base65536 / base2048 / base32768\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"chepy from_base65536; others need pip (base2048) - install only if seen.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"bifid-adfgvx\", \"concept\": \"Bifid / Trifid / ADFGX / ADFGVX / Nihilist\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"pycipher implements all; key from title; ADFGX cue is the 5/6-letter alphabet.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"mime-encoded-word\", \"concept\": \"MIME encoded-word headers\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"email.header.decode_header handles =?charset?B|Q?...?=.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"esoteric\", \"concept\": \"Brainfuc