......... octal (D6);   [0-9] 32-126 tokens -> decimal (D5); 1-26 dashed -> A1Z26\n140\t digit pairs, digits 1-5 only ..... Polybius / tap-code-digits\n141\t digit runs of 2-9 repeats ........ multitap (44 33 555); single digits 2-9 per letter -> T9\n142\t [0-9a-f] even, x2 ................ hex (D3); c1-e9/81-a9 + 40 -> EBCDIC cp037; 00 every 2nd byte -> UTF-16\n143\t . - only (+ / or 3 spaces) ....... Morse (D16: output only 0-9A-F -> hex layer; digits -> char codes); 1/111 runs -> timing\n144\t . or x knock groups .............. tap code\n145\t a/b (A/B) in 5s .................. Baconian (D17: all groups start `a` -> values 0-15 = HEX nibbles, 2 per byte);\n146\t                                    values up to 25 -> letters; odd casing in cover text -> Bacon via case\n147\t ANY 16-symbol output (0-9A-F, a-p only, 16 words) after a carrier = hex nibbles -> fromhex (D16, D17)\n148\t only A D F G X (V) ............... ADFGX / ADFGVX (keyed: try title word + crib)\n149\t only A C G T ..................... DNA 2-bit / codon\n150\t %XX .............................. URL (D7);  &#..; -> HTML (D8);  \\uXXXX -> JSON (D9);  \\xNN -> C escape\n151\t U+XXXX / %uXXXX / \\U0000XXXX ..... Unicode code-point notation -> chr(int(h,16))\n152\t =XX tokens / soft \"=\\n\" .......... quoted-printable;  =?UTF-8?B?..?= -> MIME header\n153\t A-Z2-7 (=) ....................... base32 (D10);  0-9A-V -> base32hex\n154\t A-Za-z0-9+/ (=), len%4==0 ........ base64 (D1); starts H4sI -> gzip, eJ -> zlib inside (lib.decode.peel)\n155\t A-Za-z0-9-_ no = ................. base64url (D11)\n156\t [0-9A-Za-z] only, no pad ......... base62 (x1.34) / base36 if one case (x1.55)\n157\t no 0 O I l + / = ................. base58 (x1.37)\n158\t 0-9A-Z plus space $%*+-./: ....... base45 (x1.5)\n159\t ! .. u (+z), maybe <~ ~> ......... ascii85;  RFC1924 set (no quotes , . / : [ \\ ]) -> base85; .-:+=^!/*?&<>()[]{}@%$# -> Z85\n160\t ~all printable, no ' - \\ ......... basE91 (x1.23);  ! .. } minus \" ` -> base92\n161\t begin 644 / lines start M or h ... uuencode / xxencode\n162\t xn-- labels ...................... punycode/IDNA\n163\tNON-ASCII:\n164\t U+2800-28FF ⠝⠊⠉⠑ ................. Braille (⠼ = number sign)\n165\t fullwidth Ｎｉｃｅ / math 𝐍𝐢𝐜𝐞 / ⓝ .. NFKC normalize\n166\t ɐ q ɔ p ǝ ɟ ƃ ɥ ᴉ ʞ ɯ ɹ ʇ ʌ ʍ ʎ ...... upside-down (chepy from_upside_down, then maybe [::-1])\n167\t CJK U+7Cxx, spaces kept .......... ROT8000 (chepy rot_8000)\n168\t dense CJK/Hangul, no spaces ...... base65536/base2048;  all emoji 1 per byte -> base100\n169\t invisible U+200B/C/D/2060/FEFF ... zero-width stego (count them: len(t) vs visible)\n170\t ASCII-looking with odd bytes ..... homoglyphs (Cyrillic а е о р с х)\n171\tSAME LENGTH, LETTERS ONLY CHANGE (word lengths 4 4 8 4 6! ... kept):\n172\t best rot-N English ............... Caesar (D2 rot13, D14 +7); digits also shifted by 5 -> ROT18/ROT5\n173\t mirror a<->z ..................... Atbash (D13)\n174\t crib c-p constant ratio .......... affine (lib _fit_affine); constant per position mod k -> Vigenere key = (c-p)\n175\t crib c+p periodic ................ Beaufort; no period but primer then plaintext -> autokey\n176\t crib map consistent, not affine .. keyword substitution (21 letters from crib)\n177\t neighbour keys (Muvr eptl) ....... QWERTY shift;  ;,.' inside words -> Dvorak/Colemak layout\n178\tEVERY PRINTABLE CHANGES, SPACES KEPT: ROT47 (D15) | ROT8000 | qwerty shift\n179\tSAME CHARACTER MULTISET (anagram: one ! , :, slug digits intact):\n180\t rail fence (2-6+, offset) | scytale/columnar (key = title word) | Caesar box/route | whole reverse (D12) | wordrev\n181\tWORDS: Alfa Bravo -> NATO;  -ay endings -> Pig Latin;  N1c3 w0rk -> leet;  Ook./+-<>[] -> esoteric program\n182\tTitle pun -> key: a cipher name + a word in the title/prompt = the key; verify on the crib, never guess blind.\n183\tMastery: line k = day k's codec; keyed lines restart the key per line. STACKS (D16-17): output not English but hex/digits/b32/a-p -> decode AGAIN.\n184\tSolver: return on the first full slug; joint/peel fallbacks only on a miss (D17 Mastery 83x17 died at 60 s).\n185\t```\n186\t\n187\t## Readiness gaps\n188\t\n189\t```json\n190\t[\n191\t  {\"id\": \"two-symbol-groups\", \"concept\": \"generic two-symbol fixed-width group carrier (a/b, A/B, 0/1, X/O, emoji pair, case pattern; width 4-8)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Generalize D17 `_baconhex` into lib.decode_chunk: strict branch when the fragment has exactly 2 non-space symbols (excluding Morse `.`/`-`), try both symbol->bit assignments and widths 4-8 dividing the bit count, then value ranges: all <16 + even count -> hex nibbles -> fromhex; <26 -> Bacon-26 (24 if better bigram); 32-126 -> ASCII. Fixtures: single blob + Mastery line-17-sized fragment (14 groups), upper/lower symbols, swapped polarity.\"},\n192\t  {\"id\": \"bacon-hex-lib\", \"concept\": \"Bacon-over-hex (GM-confirmed D17) as a lib decode_chunk branch + DAYS entry\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D17 lives only in the solver (`_baconhex`, register_free('baconhex',17)). Add a strict `decode_chunk` branch ([ab ]+ only, 5-groups, values <16 -> fromhex) gated by _max_day()>=17, a warmups_codecs.DAYS[17] exact encoder, and run the D17 Mastery cases (83x17) under 1.5 s total.\"},\n193\t  {\"id\": \"binary-nibbles-hex\", \"concept\": \"4-bit binary groups (`0100 1110 ...`) carrying hex nibbles\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"The next 'sixteen' carrier: [01]{4} groups, single spaces, two per byte; distinguish from 8-bit binary by group width. Also the no-space variant (len%8==0 is ambiguous with 8-bit -> both decode to the same bytes, fine).\"},\n194\t  {\"id\": \"ap-letter-hex\", \"concept\": \"hex written with the 16 letters a-p (nibble = ord-97), standalone or as a carrier's output\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D17's middle layer (Bacon-26 -> a-p). Strict branch: only [a-p], even length, no Engli